The corpus holds 600 tickets. That is a sample, not a year.
Triage takes 1.75 minutes at $34.0/hour, so one
ticket costs $0.992 to handle by hand.

Building it: 12 days at $520 = $6,240, plus running costs.

  tickets/year   manual cost   saved at 80%      payback   verdict
           200           198            159   39.3 years   do not build
         2,000         1,983          1,587    3.9 years   marginal
        20,000        19,833         15,867    0.4 years   build it
       200,000       198,333        158,667    0.0 years   build it
     1,000,000       991,667        793,333    0.0 years   build it

Same task. Same accuracy. Same everything except how often it happens.
Volume decides this, and volume is a question you can answer in an afternoon
without writing a line of code.
